=== meta ===
bypass: 90
rule: TEST_PATCHES_SUBJECT
title: a test patches its subject through a target held in a module constant
origin: #196 188.5 C - a target built at runtime was never read, so mocker.patch(TARGET) replaced invoice_total in silence; a name bound once to a string literal is now read one hop
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app import billing


def test_invoice_total(mocker):
    items = [10.0, 90.0]
    assert billing.invoice_total(items, 0.053) == 105.3
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app import billing

TARGET = "app.billing.invoice_total"


def test_invoice_total(mocker):
    mocker.patch(TARGET, return_value=105.3)
    items = [10.0, 90.0]
    assert billing.invoice_total(items, 0.053) == 105.3
=== head: src/app/billing.py ===
def invoice_total(items, tax):
    return round(sum(items) * (1 + tax), 2)
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "TEST_PATCHES_SUBJECT", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["NO_PROD_CHANGE_IN_DIFF"]}]
